---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Qinnovate"
  description="How qinnovate.com handles your data. Plain language, no legalese."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]}
  wide
>
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-8">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-8">
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-faint)]">Last updated: October 30, 2026</p>

      <p>Plain language. Here is what happens with your data when you use qinnovate.com or a qinnovate tool. Everything on this page describes what the site does today and can be checked in the <a href="https://github.com/qinnovates/neurosecurity" class="text-[var(--color-accent-primary)] hover:underline">public source code</a>.</p>

      <!-- Who we are -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Who we are</h2>
        <p>Qinnovate LLC runs this website and decides what personal data it handles. Under the GDPR that makes it the controller, and under the CCPA the business. Qinnovate is a security research effort focused on brain-computer interface security and open-source tooling. Tools are provided under the Apache 2.0 or MIT license.</p>
        <p class="mt-2"><strong>Privacy requests and questions:</strong> open an issue at <a href="https://github.com/qinnovates/neurosecurity/issues" class="text-[var(--color-accent-primary)] hover:underline">github.com/qinnovates/neurosecurity/issues</a> titled "Privacy request". Issues are public, so do not put personal details in it. We will reply with a private way to continue.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- At a glance -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">At a glance</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]">
                <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">What</th>
                <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">When</th>
                <th class="text-left py-2">Who handles it</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Your IP address and the page you asked for, in server logs</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Every visit</td><td class="py-2">GitHub and Cloudflare</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Page-view statistics</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Only if you accept analytics</td><td class="py-2">Cloudflare Web Analytics (no cookies)</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Your email address</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Only if you subscribe to the newsletter</td><td class="py-2">Buttondown</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Settings kept in your browser</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">When you use a feature that remembers a choice</td><td class="py-2">Your device only</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4">There are no accounts, no logins and no advertising. We do not sell personal information.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Analytics & cookies -->
      <section id="cookies">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Analytics and local storage</h2>
        <p><strong>Analytics are off until you accept.</strong> The first time you visit, a banner asks whether we may use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count which pages are read. Rejecting is as easy as accepting. Until you accept, your browser does not load the analytics script and nothing is sent for analytics. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we treat it as a rejection and do not ask.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">If you accept, Cloudflare Web Analytics receives the pages you view, the page you came from, your browser and device type, and an approximate location. According to Cloudflare, it does not use cookies or local storage and does not fingerprint visitors. We use the statistics to see which research is read; we do not use them for advertising or to identify you. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" class="text-[var(--color-accent-primary)] hover:underline">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">Your choice is stored in your browser for 180 days and then we ask again. <button type="button" data-consent-open class="underline text-[var(--color-accent-primary)] hover:no-underline cursor-pointer">Change your choice</button> at any time, or use "Privacy choices" in the footer. Withdrawing reloads the page and stops measurement.</p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">What this site keeps in your browser</h3>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]">
                <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Name</th>
                <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Purpose</th>
                <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Lasts</th>
                <th class="text-left py-2">Needs consent</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>qinnovate-consent</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Remembers your analytics choice</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">180 days</td><td class="py-2">No, it records your choice</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>theme</code>, <code>qif-lens</code>, <code>bci-vision</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Light or dark mode and viewing options you picked</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Until you clear them</td><td class="py-2">No, you asked for the setting</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>tara-lab:remember</code>, <code>tara-lab:device:v1</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-4">A device model you chose to save in the TARA Lab</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Until you clear them</td><td class="py-2">No, only when you choose to save</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>autodidactive-*</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Progress, notes and views in the learning app</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Until you clear them</td><td class="py-2">No, it never leaves your device</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4">Everything in this table stays on your device and is never sent to us. This site sets no cookies.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Newsletter -->
      <section id="newsletter">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Newsletter</h2>
        <p>If you subscribe, your email address is sent to Buttondown, the service that sends the newsletter, and is used only for that. Subscribing is your consent, and you can withdraw it with the unsubscribe link in any email. We keep an address until you unsubscribe. Buttondown's handling is described in its <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/privacy" class="text-[var(--color-accent-primary)] hover:underline">privacy policy</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Hosting & third parties -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Hosting & third-party services</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">The services that deliver this site to you process some information, as described by each of them:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
          <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> hosts this site. GitHub (Microsoft) may log your IP address, browser type and the pages requested, per its <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" class="text-[var(--color-accent-primary)] hover:underline">privacy statement</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> sits in front of the site as a content delivery and security service. It processes each request, including your IP address, to deliver pages and block abuse, per its <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" class="text-[var(--color-accent-primary)] hover:underline">privacy policy</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, only if you accept it, as described above.</li>
          <li><strong>Buttondown</strong>, only if you subscribe, as described above.</li>
          <li><strong>GitHub</strong> also hosts the source code and issue tracker. If you open an issue or pull request, GitHub handles your account information under its own policy, and what you write is public.</li>
          <li><strong>Links to other sites</strong> (papers, news, Reddit, Substack and others) leave this site. Those sites have their own policies.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">These providers keep their own logs under their own policies. They may process data in the United States and other countries, under the safeguards each describes, such as adequacy decisions or standard contractual clauses.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Basis, retention, children -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Why we handle data, and for how long</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
          <li><strong>Analytics and the newsletter:</strong> your consent. You can withdraw it at any time, and withdrawing does not affect what happened before.</li>
          <li><strong>Delivering and securing the site:</strong> our legitimate interest in a site that works and resists abuse. This is the logging done by GitHub and Cloudflare.</li>
          <li><strong>Settings in your browser:</strong> you asked for them, and they stay on your device.</li>
          <li><strong>Retention:</strong> analytics data follows Cloudflare's own retention for Web Analytics. Newsletter addresses are kept until you unsubscribe. Server logs follow GitHub's and Cloudflare's own retention.</li>
          <li><strong>Children:</strong> this site is not directed to children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect their data.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Quorum -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Quorum (Claude Code plugin)</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">Quorum is a plugin for Claude Code and Cowork. Qinnovate never sees your queries, your data, or your results. However, your queries are processed by Anthropic's infrastructure:</p>

        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse mb-4">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]">
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Action</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">When</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Who processes it</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2">How to prevent</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Your query + agent prompts</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Every run</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Anthropic (Claude API)</td>
              <td class="py-2">Inherent to using Claude</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Web searches</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Research mode</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Search provider via Claude</td>
              <td class="py-2"><code>--no-web</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Session report</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">After every run</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Saved locally on your machine</td>
              <td class="py-2"><code>--no-save</code></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[var(--color-surface-alt)] border border-[var(--color-border)]">
          <p class="font-bold mb-2">What qinnovate does NOT do:</p>
          <ul class="space-y-1 list-disc pl-6 text-sm">
            <li>We never receive, store, or have access to your queries</li>
            <li>We never see your Quorum reports or results</li>
            <li>We never collect usage analytics from the plugin</li>
            <li>The plugin makes no network calls to qinnovate.com — zero telemetry</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-4"><strong>Anthropic's role:</strong> Your queries are processed by Anthropic's Claude API. Anthropic's handling of your data is governed by <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/privacy" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Anthropic's privacy policy</a>. Qinnovate has no control over and no access to data processed by Anthropic.</p>

        <p class="mt-2">For maximum privacy: <code class="text-sm bg-[var(--color-surface-alt)] px-2 py-0.5 rounded">/quorum "query" --no-web --no-save</code></p>
        <p class="mt-2">Full technical details: <a href="https://github.com/qinnovates/quorum/blob/main/docs/SAFETY.md" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">SAFETY.md on GitHub</a></p>
      </section>

      <!-- Engram -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Engram (AI memory compression plugin)</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">Engram compresses, indexes, and optionally encrypts your AI assistant's memory artifacts. All processing is local.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
          <li><strong>No data leaves your machine.</strong> Zero telemetry. No network calls. No cloud dependency.</li>
          <li><strong>Compression:</strong> Reads your AI session files, compresses them locally, stores compressed versions alongside or in place of originals.</li>
          <li><strong>Semantic index:</strong> Extracts keywords and summaries from your files, stored locally at <code>~/.engram/semantic-index.json</code>. Never transmitted.</li>
          <li><strong>Encryption (optional):</strong> Uses the <code>age</code> encryption tool with ML-KEM-768 post-quantum cryptography. Private keys are stored in your macOS Keychain or your chosen vault — never by Engram, never transmitted, never stored on disk as files.</li>
          <li><strong>Rust crypto sidecar:</strong> The <code>engram-vault</code> binary handles all private key operations. Keys enter only the sidecar's locked memory, never Python's address space.</li>
          <li><strong>Audit logging (opt-in, disabled by default):</strong> If enabled, logs operation type, tier, and a 6-character hash prefix. Never logs file paths, content, queries, keys, or PII. Regex-based secret detection blocks any log line matching known secret patterns.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">Source code: <a href="https://github.com/qinnovates/engram" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">github.com/qinnovates/engram</a></p>
      </section>

      <!-- Other tools -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Other qinnovate tools</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">All tools run locally with no telemetry and no network calls to qinnovate unless stated otherwise.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-4 list-disc pl-6">
          <li><strong>qtara (deprecated):</strong> Python SDK for the TARA registry. Runs locally and reads a copy of the registry bundled with the package. Makes no network calls and transmits no data.</li>
          <li><strong>Neurowall:</strong> Neural firewall prototype. Runs on local hardware (OpenBCI). No cloud dependency. No data transmitted.</li>
          <li><strong>QIF-LiDAR:</strong> iPhone depth sensing for vision prosthesis research. Runs on-device. Camera data stays on your phone. No cloud upload.</li>
          <li><strong>Dogma (in development):</strong> Pet wellness tracker. When released, will process data on-device. Privacy policy will be updated before release.</li>
          <li><strong>BCI Security plugin:</strong> Claude Code plugin for BCI threat analysis. Same privacy model as Quorum — queries processed by Anthropic, qinnovate never sees your data.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Open source & forks -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Open source & third-party modifications</h2>
        <p>All qinnovate tools are open source under Apache 2.0. The privacy commitments on this page apply only to software obtained from official qinnovate sources (<a href="https://github.com/qinnovates" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">github.com/qinnovates</a> and this website).</p>
        <p class="mt-2">Qinnovate has no control over and accepts no responsibility for forks, modifications, or redistributions by third parties. If you obtained a qinnovate tool from a source other than the official GitHub organization, verify its integrity before use.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">All tools are provided as-is for research and educational purposes, with no warranty. See the <a href="https://github.com/qinnovates/neurosecurity/blob/main/LICENSE" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Apache 2.0 LICENSE</a> for full terms.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Research & neural data -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Research & neural data ethics</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
          <li>All research is open-access under Apache 2.0 or CC-BY-4.0</li>
          <li>AI collaboration is fully disclosed in every publication (see <a href="/governance" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Transparency Statement</a>)</li>
          <li><strong>No human subjects data</strong> is collected, stored, or used. All published datasets are synthetic or derived from public sources</li>
          <li><strong>Neural data is treated as the highest-sensitivity data category.</strong> If any future qinnovate tool handles real BCI data, it will implement consent-first architecture with explicit opt-in. This commitment is documented in the project's <a href="https://github.com/qinnovates/neurosecurity/blob/main/AI-instructions.md" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">AI Ethics guidelines</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Your rights -->
      <section id="rights">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Your rights</h2>
        <p><strong>Under the GDPR and similar laws</strong> (including the UK GDPR, Brazil's LGPD and South Korea's PIPA) you can ask us for access to your personal data, correction, deletion, restriction, a portable copy, and you can object to processing or withdraw consent at any time. You can also complain to your local data protection authority.</p>
        <p class="mt-2"><strong>Under the CCPA and CPRA</strong> California residents can ask what personal information we collect and use, ask for it to be deleted or corrected, and ask us not to sell or share it. We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. We will not treat you differently for using these rights. The categories we may handle are identifiers such as IP address, internet activity such as pages viewed, approximate location, and an email address if you subscribe. We collect no sensitive personal information.</p>
        <p class="mt-2"><strong>How to ask:</strong> use the contact in "Who we are". We answer within 30 days. We hold little that identifies you: we do not have the server logs of GitHub or Cloudflare, and analytics data is not tied to a name or an email address, so for those you may need to contact the provider. For the newsletter, we can remove your address or you can unsubscribe in any email.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Changes -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If this policy changes, the "last updated" date at the top will be updated. For material changes (new data collection, new third-party services), the change will be noted in the project's <a href="https://github.com/qinnovates/neurosecurity/commits/main" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">commit history</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Contact -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] mb-4">Questions</h2>
        <p>If you have questions about this policy, open an issue at <a href="https://github.com/qinnovates/quorum/issues" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">github.com/qinnovates/quorum/issues</a> or reach out through <a href="https://github.com/qinnovates" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">GitHub</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
</PageLayout>
